>> title: Ras el Hanout
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: moroccan, spice blend, toasted, pantry
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: ras al hanout, rass el hanout
>> pairs-with: lamb-tagine
>> servings: 24
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — the whole spices toast three minutes and everything already ground goes in off the heat, because ground spice on a hot pan is scorched before it smells of anything; a blend this long has no single flavour to hide a burn behind
>> step.1: toast in a dry skillet 3 min
>> step.2: add off the heat
>> step.3: cool, grind fine
>> step.4: whisk in

Toast @coriander seeds{2%Tbs}(12 g), @cumin seeds{1%Tbs}(6 g), @black peppercorns{2%tsp}, @allspice berries{1%tsp}, @cloves{1%tsp}, and @green cardamom pods{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until fragrant, about ~{3%min}.

Add @cinnamon stick{1}(3-in piece, broken up) and @dried rosebuds{1%Tbs}(petals only) to @&(~1)toasted spices{} off the heat.

Cool @&(~1)spices{} completely, then grind to a fine powder in a #spice grinder{}.

Whisk @ground turmeric{2%tsp}, @ground ginger{2%tsp}, and @freshly grated nutmeg{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)powder{}.
